#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Learn which time-based usage fields in the IBM Quantum Compute API to "
"disregard, and which resource unit (RU) fields replace them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate to resource units (RUs) in the IBM Quantum Compute API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate to resource units (RUs) in the IBM Quantum Compute API {#migrate-to-"
"resource-units-rus-in-the-ibm-quantum-compute-api}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum&reg; Platform now measures usage in resource units (RUs). An RU "
"is the unit that IBM Quantum uses to measure and bill the usage of all "
"workloads. Before this change, the platform measured usage as QPU time in "
"seconds or milliseconds. For more information about RUs, see [Resource "
"units](/guides/plans-overview#resource-units).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Today, the API returns two sets of fields: the old time fields and the new "
"RU fields. Your integration continues to work. In a future release, IBM "
"Quantum will remove the time fields. Change your integration to read the RU "
"fields now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This guide uses these terms:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Workload**: A job, a session, a batch, or a function run.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**QPU workload**: A job, a session, or a batch. A QPU workload runs only on "
"a QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Function workload**: A function run. A function workload can use classical"
" compute and an execution license, and it can also use a QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Session**: A group of jobs that run together on one QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Instance**: A service instance. It owns workloads and has usage limits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Plan**: The service plan of an account. It sets the usage limits for all "
"instances in the account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  This guide uses version 0.57.2 of the [OpenAPI spec](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/openapi.json).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The `IBM-API-Version` header value must be `2026-04-15` or a later supported API version.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Endpoint | Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `GET /v1/jobs`, `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics` | `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/workloads` | `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"
"| `POST /v1/sessions`, `GET /v1/sessions/{id}` | `elapsed_time` | `usage.value` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/instances/usage` | `usage_consumed_seconds`, `usage_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `usage_consumed_ru`, `usage_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/accounts/{id}` | `plans[].usage_limit_seconds`, `plans[].usage_allocation_seconds`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_seconds` | `plans[].usage_limit_ru`, `plans[].usage_allocation_ru`, `plans[].unallocated_usage_ru` |\n"
"| Resource Controller API: Create, update, and read service instances | `instance_limit_seconds`, `usage_allocation_seconds` | `instance_limit_ru`, `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `GET /v1/analytics/usage`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped_by_date` | Each usage field in milliseconds | The matching field with the `_ru` suffix |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The sections that follow give the details for each endpoint.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Jobs {#jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints: `GET /v1/jobs` and `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The `usage` object also has these fields:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage.unit`: The unit of `usage.value`. The value is always "
"`\"resource_units\"`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage.status`: The billing status. The value is `\"pending\"` or "
"`\"complete\"`. If the status is `\"pending\"`, the platform can still "
"change the value. Do not use a pending value as the final usage.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage.details[]`: The usage for each billing metric. The `value` of each "
"entry is in RUs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The field `usage.details[].metric.value` is not the usage in RUs. It is the "
"quantity of the metric that the platform used to calculate the RUs. Each "
"metric has its own unit. For example, the unit of a QPU metric is seconds. "
"For the usage, read `usage.details[].value`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Workloads {#workloads}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint: `GET /v1/workloads`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each item in `workloads[]` has a `usage` object. This object has the same "
"fields as the `usage` object of a job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `workloads[].usage.qpu_charge_time_seconds` | `workloads[].usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If a workload is still running, `usage` is `null`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Function workloads {#function-workloads}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The usage of a function workload is in RUs, the same as for a QPU workload. "
"A function workload can use more than one metric:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**QPU usage.** This is metered per second of quantum time. See [Execution "
"modes](/guides/execution-modes).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Classical compute usage.** This is metered per second of [classical "
"time](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Execution license cost.** This is metered per workload, based on the [size"
" of the problem passed to a function](/guides/functions#overview-of-"
"available-functions).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The platform converts the quantity of each metric to RUs. Thus, all usage "
"values are in RUs:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.value` is the usage of the workload, in RUs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`usage.details[].value` is the usage for one metric, in RUs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage.details[].metric.value` is the quantity of the metric, in the unit of"
" that metric. It is not in RUs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you show or add usage values, use `usage.value` and "
"`usage.details[].value`. Do not use `usage.details[].metric.value`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sessions {#sessions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints: `POST /v1/sessions` and `GET /v1/sessions/{id}`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `elapsed_time` (seconds) | `usage.value` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The session `usage` object has `unit` and `details[]`. These fields work the"
" same as in the job `usage` object, with the exception of the `status` "
"field, which is omitted for sessions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fields `interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl`, and `active_ttl` do not change. "
"They are time limits (TTL means \"time to live\"), not usage. Their unit "
"stays seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Instance usage {#instance-usage}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint: `GET /v1/instances/usage`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `usage_consumed_seconds` | `usage_consumed_ru` |\n"
"| `usage_limit_seconds` | `usage_limit_ru` |\n"
"| `usage_allocation_seconds` | `usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fields `usage_limit_reached`, `usage_period`, and `time_available_at` do"
" not change.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account plans {#account-plans}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint: `GET /v1/accounts/{id}`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Each item in `plans[]` has these changes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard | Read instead |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `plans[].usage_limit_seconds` | `plans[].usage_limit_ru` |\n"
"| `plans[].usage_allocation_seconds` | `plans[].usage_allocation_ru` |\n"
"| `plans[].unallocated_usage_seconds` | `plans[].unallocated_usage_ru` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Service instances in the Resource Controller API {#service-instances-in-the-"
"resource-controller-api}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The IBM Cloud&reg; Resource Controller API is a separate API. You use it to "
"create and update service instances. If you create or update instances with "
"this API, change the instance parameters too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you create or update an instance, send these parameters in the "
"request:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Don't send | Send instead | Type of the new parameter |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| `instance_limit_seconds` | `instance_limit_ru` | Number or `null` |\n"
"| `usage_allocation_seconds` | `usage_allocation_ru` | Number or `null` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The parameters have these meanings:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Instance limit**The maximum usage for the instance. If you do not send a "
"limit on the Open Plan, the default is the RU equivalent of 10 minutes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Usage allocation**: The share of usage for the instance. The fair-share "
"scheduler uses this value to set the priority of the instance in the queue. "
"The allocation does not apply to Pay-As-You-Go instances.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you read an instance, the `extensions` object in the response contains "
"the old fields and the new fields. Disregard `instance_limit_seconds` and "
"`usage_allocation_seconds`. Read `instance_limit_ru` and "
"`usage_allocation_ru`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more information, see the [IBM Quantum Compute Service REST API "
"documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-runtime-rest).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Usage analytics {#usage-analytics}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Endpoints: `GET /v1/analytics/usage`, `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped`, and"
" `GET /v1/analytics/usage_grouped_by_date`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The three endpoints have the same usage fields. The two grouped endpoints "
"return these fields for each group or each date.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The old analytics usage fields are in milliseconds, not seconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Disregard (milliseconds) | Read instead (RUs) |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `usage` | `usage_ru` |\n"
"| `sessions_usage` | `sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `avg_sessions_usage` | `avg_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `max_sessions_usage` | `max_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `batch_sessions_usage` | `batch_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `avg_batch_sessions_usage` | `avg_batch_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `max_batch_sessions_usage` | `max_batch_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `dedicated_sessions_usage` | `dedicated_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `avg_dedicated_sessions_usage` | `avg_dedicated_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `max_dedicated_sessions_usage` | `max_dedicated_sessions_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `individual_jobs_usage` | `individual_jobs_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `avg_individual_jobs_usage` | `avg_individual_jobs_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `max_individual_jobs_usage` | `max_individual_jobs_usage_ru` |\n"
"| `functions_quantum_usage_ms` | `functions_quantum_usage_ru` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These function fields are new. They have no old field in milliseconds:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`functions_usage_ru`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`avg_functions_usage_ru`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`max_functions_usage_ru`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`functions_classical_usage_ru`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`functions_license_cost_ru`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The total in `usage_ru` includes more than the total in `usage`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage` is the sum of QPU time for sessions, individual jobs, and "
"functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`usage_ru` is the sum of usage for sessions, individual jobs, and functions."
" For functions, it also includes classical compute and license cost.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, `usage_ru` is not only `usage` in a different unit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fields `queue_time`, `avg_queue_time`, and `max_queue_time` do not "
"change. They measure wait time, not usage. Their unit stays milliseconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fields that do not change {#fields-that-do-not-change}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These fields contain time values, but they do not measure usage. IBM Quantum"
" does not plan to replace them:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_time_seconds` on backends: The estimated wait in the queue.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`circuits_execution_time_ns` in `GET /v1/jobs/{id}/metrics`: The time that "
"the job ran on the QPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`interactive_ttl`, `max_ttl`, and `active_ttl` on sessions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`queue_time`, `avg_queue_time`, and `max_queue_time` in analytics.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`rep_times` and `circuit_duration` in backend configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Migration steps {#migration-steps}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Find each old field in your code. Search for `qpu_charge_time_seconds`, "
"`elapsed_time`, the `_seconds` fields in this guide, and the analytics "
"fields in milliseconds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change each old field to the RU field in the tables of this guide.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you create or update service instances with the Resource Controller API, "
"send `instance_limit_ru` and `usage_allocation_ru`. Do not send the "
"`_seconds` parameters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Change the labels in your user interface. Show \"RU\" or \"resource units\","
" not \"seconds\" or \"minutes\". Do not convert RUs to time. There is no "
"fixed rate between RUs and time.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you read `usage.details[]`, use `value` for the usage in RUs. Do not use "
"`metric.value`, because its unit is the unit of the metric.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If `usage.status` is `\"pending\"`, show the value as provisional.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If an RU field is missing or `null`, use the same logic that you use for the"
" old field today.\n"
msgstr ""
